---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PrivacyBadge from '../../components/PrivacyBadge.astro';
import JsonLd from '../../components/JsonLd.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Resize Image Locally — Change Pixel Dimensions | ZeroSend" description="Resize JPG, PNG, and WebP image dimensions directly in your browser. Preserve aspect ratio and download without a file-processing upload.">
  <JsonLd data={{ '@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'WebApplication', name:'ZeroSend Image Resizer', applicationCategory:'UtilitiesApplication', isAccessibleForFree:true }} />
  <section class="tool-page"><div class="container narrow-wide"><p class="eyebrow">IMAGE TOOL</p><h1>Image Resizer</h1><p class="lead">Change width and height in pixels while keeping the work on your device.</p><PrivacyBadge />
    <div class="tool-shell" data-resizer><label class="dropzone"><strong>Choose an image</strong><span>JPG, PNG or WebP</span><input type="file" accept="image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp" /></label><div class="controls hidden" data-controls><div class="two-fields"><label>Width (px)<input data-width type="number" min="1" max="8192" step="1" /></label><label>Height (px)<input data-height type="number" min="1" max="8192" step="1" /></label></div><label class="check"><input data-lock type="checkbox" checked /> Keep aspect ratio</label><label>Quality for JPG/WebP <output data-quality-output>90%</output><input data-quality type="range" min="10" max="100" value="90" /></label><button class="button primary" data-process type="button">Resize image</button></div><p class="status" data-status id="tool-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p><div class="result hidden" data-result><img data-preview alt="Preview of resized image" /><div class="stats"><div><span>Original</span><strong data-original-dim></strong></div><div><span>Result</span><strong data-result-dim></strong></div><div><span>File size</span><strong data-result-size></strong></div></div><a class="button primary" data-download download>Download resized image</a></div></div>
    <article class="content-block"><h2>How to resize an image locally</h2><ol><li>Select your image.</li><li>Enter a new width or height.</li><li>Keep aspect ratio enabled to avoid stretching.</li><li>Resize and download the result.</li></ol><h2>When should you resize?</h2><p>Reducing pixel dimensions can dramatically reduce transfer size and memory use when an image is larger than its display target.</p><h2>Limits and browser support</h2><p>JPG, PNG and WebP inputs are limited to 25 MiB, 8192 pixels per side and 16 megapixels total. The WebP converter accepts JPG and PNG only. A smaller image may be needed on phones with limited memory. Unsupported encoders report an error. Animated images become a single still frame; metadata and color profiles may change. Transparent pixels become white when exporting JPG.</p><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>Does resizing crop the image?</h3><p>No. This tool scales the full image to the requested dimensions. Cropping will be a separate tool.</p><h3>Can enlarging improve detail?</h3><p>No. Increasing dimensions creates more pixels but cannot recover detail that is absent from the source.</p><h2>Related tools</h2><p><a href="/tools/image-compressor">Image Compressor</a> · <a href="/tools/jpg-png-to-webp">JPG / PNG to WebP</a></p></article>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<script>
  import { initImageTool } from '../../scripts/image-tool';
  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-resizer]');
  if (root) initImageTool(root, 'resize');
</script>
